00:00.000 --> 00:06.240
Imagine you have just formalized a genuinely original idea, like something you spent years

00:06.240 --> 00:14.000
developing, and you decide to email this insight to a world-famous thinger who works in your exact

00:14.000 --> 00:20.280
niche. So you hit send. A very hopeful moment. Exactly. Very hopeful. But then your carefully

00:20.280 --> 00:24.680
constructed argument just immediately vanishes. It goes into an inbox that is currently receiving,

00:24.680 --> 00:32.080
you know, tens of thousands of basic FAQs, literal spam, and people aggressively repeating the exact

00:32.080 --> 00:37.040
same debunked argument. Yeah, it's brutal. It is. You're essentially just a drop of signal in an

00:37.040 --> 00:42.520
absolute ocean of noise. And I mean, what you're describing there is a complete structural failure

